{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p3-b4096c72","text":"For the cardio card: `.ae-card-head` has `align-items: baseline` and `margin: 10px 0 16px`. The user says the texts should stay left/right but be centered (like km and minutes are in the stats box). In the card, the stats boxes have `ae-stat-box` column centered. Hmm "eles devem estar no centro (como o km e os minutos)" — vertically centered? In the card, the CARDIO line is a row; visually the label and name might be misaligned relative to each other due to baseline + different text heights? Actually both same font-size, so baseline alignment is fine.

Wait — maybe the issue: In the card, `.ae-card-head` is a flex row with `align-items: baseline` while the card body is `display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items: center`? Then justify-content: space-between + width 100% gives left/right. What "centro" means? "eles devem continuar um na esquerda e um na direita, entretanto eles devem estar no centro (como o km e os minutos)" — the km/minutes are in `.ae-card-stats` which is centered horizontally as a group (justify-content: center). Hmm, km and minutes are two boxes centered in the card. So maybe they mean the CARDIO line should be centered as a group? No — they said left and right.

Alternatively "no centro" = vertically centered relative to the row (aligned with each other). With `align-items: baseline`, if one wraps to two lines, they'd misalign. For the table, `align-items: baseline` similar.

Hmm, let me look at the actual rendering. Maybe the problem is that the CARDIO label/name in the CARD are positioned at the very top-left/right while the km/min boxes are centered, and the visual issue is the head is not aligned to the body width? Hmm.

Let me check the live UI to see. Since the app is at the Ficha tab, let me navigate there and inspect the cardio card. Actually there might be no cardio in test mode. Let me check quickly in the browser: click Treino tab → Ficha.

But first: maybe the real issue is that the label and type are not vertically centered within their row because of `align-items: baseline` when the type name wraps (long name like "Bicicleta Ergométrica"). The type has `overflow-wrap: anywhere` and can wrap to 2 lines, so the label stays on the first baseline at top while the row is taller. "devem estar no centro" = vertically centered in the row.

Hmm, but "como o km e os minutos" — the km/min values are centered inside their boxes. So vertical centering.

Hold on. Maybe the complaint relates to the *table* row where the CARDIO/type line occupies a narrow cell, and the text isn't vertically centered relative to the Vel/Tempo text? Hmm.

I need to see the actual UI. Let me navigate to the workout tab and find the cardio card, then measure positions of the label, type, and the stat boxes.

